{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1418785-questions-about-motifs","id":1418785,"title":"Questions about Motifs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-18T01:44:19-07:00","id":1418785,"title":"Questions about Motifs","content":"Hello, <br /> <br /> I have two questions about Motifs : <br /> <br /> - I don't understand how the custom motifs work with the specialized purviews of Passion and Beasts. For Passions, p256, &quot;In exchange, you may create a motif based on the chosen emotion, which you can use to work marvels with any Purview&quot;. I'm a Scion of Hel, with the Passion (Fear) purview, how this works concretly ? What should I do to use, for example, my Fire Purview ? <br /> <br /> - Does Motifs are required to use purchased boons ? Or only for marvels ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26497-varkal","name":"Varkal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T04:13:06-07:00","id":1418800,"title":"","content":"For the second question, motifs are only for Marvels. For the first question, you think up a motif based off the specialization and you can use that motif for any Purview you have access to, for example for your Scion of Hel example they could have the motif of \u201cTerror of the grave\u201d which you can use for Marvels to invoke fear and terror of dying or pain, including for the Fire Purview like invoking the fear of firery deaths","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T07:49:03-07:00","id":1418824,"title":"","content":"Shiva and Kali have Artistry (Dance), so they can use dance to create Marvels with any of their Purviews.<br /> <br /> Artistry is admittedly the easiest of those three to think up.<br /> <br /> To use the Hel example she presumably has a motif based on all encompassing dread, so through behaving in a terrifying manner she can terrify up a Marvel of any of her Purviews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T08:27:31-07:00","id":1418830,"title":"","content":"So, each pantheon has their motifs to work marvels through. The theoi ask their fam for favours, the deva undergo austerities etc etc. Taking a specialised purview (NOT, I stress, the kind in Mysteries of the World, just looked that up) gives you a second aspect you can channel those marvels through. As part of the Aesir by default you can chuck some runestones or chant a galdr to (for example) fill an NPC with uncanny panic (i.e. a complication or impose condition marvel). Your average Hero is stuck with only that but by taking the Passion (Fear) specialty you can make up a relevant statement (Similar to birthright relics) to use as a alternative channel. Note that as Magicjohnny said this isn't limited to the source purview, you can channel your Fire marvels through it as well.<br /> <br /> Decidedly inexhaustive selection of examples: You could work the same &quot;inflict panic&quot; type spell through telling a decent ghost story, or (to borrow Magicjohnny's example) whisper your intentions into a handful of grave dirt, or some other symbolic representation of the fear of death. Or maybe you could draw on your/someone else's existing fear to power a different marvel. At this point I feel like it becomes a question of how liberal your Storyguide is with interpretation of your chosen motif.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26056-cassiecataria","name":"CassieCataria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}